course: dictionary
lesson: 10077
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and thaw is a good example. Read the words around it to find the right meaning. «The Arctic woolly bear caterpillar freezes solid each winter and thaws in summer.» Here thaws means it stops being frozen and becomes soft again.
explain: Thaw can also be a noun, which is a name for a time: «a thaw» is a spell of warmer weather when snow and ice melt. Thaw is a verb when it describes an action, as in thaws, thawed and thawing.
explain: People can thaw too. If someone «thawed a little», they did not turn into ice water. They became friendlier after being cold to you. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Thaw means to melt, or to become soft again after being frozen.
fact: Thaw out and defrost both mean to stop being frozen.
fact: A thaw is a warmer time when snow and ice melt, such as a spring thaw.
fact: Frozen meat must be thawed in the fridge, not left out, which keeps it safe to eat.
fact: The wood frog can freeze solid in winter and thaw and hop away in spring.
exercise: «The Arctic woolly bear caterpillar freezes solid each winter and thaws in summer.» What does thaws mean here? | Gets harder and colder | Hides under a leaf until winter ends | *Stops being frozen and becomes soft again
exercise: «Water expands when it freezes, which can split a pipe; when it thaws, water pours out.» What does thaws mean? | Freezes into a solid block | Turns into a cloud | *Melts and becomes liquid again
exercise: «In spring the thaw made the river rise.» What is a thaw? | A cold wind from the north | A fish that lives under ice | *A warmer time when snow and ice melt
test: Ben says, «She thawed a little after I said sorry.» What does thawed mean in this sentence? | She was frozen solid | She melted into a puddle | *She became friendlier after being cold
test: Mia reads that frozen mice are thawed before a snake eats them. Which word means the same as thawed here? | *Defrosted, so they are soft and unfrozen | Heated up until they cook | Hidden in a box
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Permafrost stays frozen all year, but in summer only a thin top layer thaws into mud»? | Freezes harder | *Melts and becomes soft | Turns into a bird | Grows into a tree
